{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.FeynmanClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.FeynmanClassicalLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.classicalLimitStpart_not_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.classicalLimitStpart_not_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/feynman-classical-limit.lean#L64-L69","doc":"The class is not trivially inhabited: an evaluator with\n`jones 0 1 = 0` admits no instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.feynman_classical_limit_g3_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.feynman_classical_limit_g3_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/feynman-classical-limit.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**Conditional on `conj:classical-limit-stpart`.** At `q = 1` the\nJones evaluator cannot distinguish two knots. Derived from the class\nhypothesis (both values equal `1`), not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.ClassicalLimitStpart.jones_trivial_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.ClassicalLimitStpart.jones_trivial_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/feynman-classical-limit.lean#L54-L54","doc":"In the `q → 1` limit every knot's Jones value collapses to `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.ClassicalLimitStpart.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.ClassicalLimitStpart.mk","kind":"ctor","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/feynman-classical-limit.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.ClassicalLimitStpart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanClassicalLimit.ConditionalAudit.ClassicalLimitStpart","kind":"class","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/feynman-classical-limit.lean#L36-L54","doc":"**§3b-cond hypothesis class** for `conj:classical-limit-stpart`.\n\nThe classical-limit functor is the standard-part of evaluation at\n`q = 1 + ε`; in that limit the categorical trace degenerates so that\nthe Jones polynomial loses all knot-discrimination — `J_K(1) = 1`\nfor every knot `K` (clause 4 of `prop:feynman-classical-limit`).\n\nContent: for a given knot-indexed Jones evaluator `jones K q`, the\nvalue at `q = 1` is `1` for every knot. The evaluator is a parameter,\nso the class constrains it rather than asserting that some constant\nfunction exists. (Before 2026-11-16 the field read\n`∃ jonesAtOne : ℕ → ℝ, ∀ K, jonesAtOne K = 1`, which\n`⟨fun _ => 1, fun _ => rfl⟩` proves outright: a carrier that asserted\nnothing.) The full categorical degeneration is in\n`QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.ClassicalLimitDegeneration`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}